  "equipment_type": "Air-cooled scroll chiller controller",
  "applies_to": "Carrier AquaSnap 30RC 010-060 air-cooled scroll chillers (with or without Greenspeed fans) using the Carrier Controller.",
  "summary": "The 30RC's Carrier Controller provides BACnet IP on Ethernet port J5 and BACnet MS/TP on RS-485 port J10, configured from the BACnet Standard Conf. menu. Command points come as separate read (_rd) and write (_wr) objects, with the writable copies at 10000+ instances. Alarm objects are numbered after Carrier's alarm codes (e.g. BV 110001).",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "default_device_instance": 1600001,
  "notes": [
    "Command points have a read object (e.g. BV 12 GENUNIT_CHIL_S_S_rd) and a separate write object (BV 10012 GENUNIT_CHIL_S_S_wr).",
    "Many ALM_ objects have a blank description in the table; the name identifies the alarm.",
    "The table also lists a database alias name and low/high limits, not reproduced here."
  ],
